Stage 02: TIP FOLD SOLVED - all four strategies accepted 10/10 (2026-08-13)
- Mike pushed back that four independent strategies failing identically pointed at MY
  shared code, and that a working cap4 existed in git history. Both were right.
- THE ANSWER was already in this repository, commit bfaeaf1 "cap4 camber-split tip cap -
  full-resolution pyHyp march validated at L1". Its construction differs from everything
  I tried in two decisive ways:
    1. The inner boundary is built FROM THE SECTION, not from the outer ring:
       rect = camber + width_frac * (surface - camber). That is a convex combination of
       the camber line and the actual surface, so it lies inside the section BY
       CONSTRUCTION. Every one of my ~15 attempts derived the inner ring by displacing
       the outer ring (shrink, smooth, camber-offset, bisector offset, arc-length
       re-parameterisation), none of which carries that guarantee - and on a cambered
       lower surface the inner ring left the section and the patch inverted.
    2. The inner rectangle is INSET CHORDWISE, so the collar end edges slant from the
       OML corners to the rectangle corners. The original code even documents the
       failure I hit: "Without the inset, the end edges are collinear with the
       rectangle's short sides ... which degenerates the corner cells to zero Jacobian."
